cv/vault/** filter=git-crypt diff=git-crypt
*.key filter=git-crypt diff=git-crypt

# Zero-byte files must never go through a clean filter. git's
# ce_match_stat_basic() short-circuits on a zero-size worktree file: if the
# stored blob is not the empty blob it is marked DATA_CHANGED permanently, and
# the filter is never consulted. git-crypt stores even an empty file as a
# 22-byte header, never the empty blob, so such files read as dirty forever and
# pre-commit's stash/restore dies on "No valid patches in input" - every commit
# fails after all hooks have passed.
#
# These markers are empty by definition, so plaintext costs nothing: git-crypt
# never encrypted paths anyway, and its deterministic nonce means an empty file
# is already identifiable from its fixed 22-byte ciphertext.
#
# A later line overrides an earlier one, so these must stay below the rules
# above. `!filter` unsets the attribute; `-filter` would set it to false.
# Real source files should be given content rather than an exception here; the
# git-crypt-empty-guard hook in flake.nix enforces that and explains it when a
# new empty file trips over it.
# Refs: pre-commit#776, git-crypt#53, git-crypt PR#210.
cv/vault/**/.codex !filter !diff
